From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Anthony Fu (via agent)" <reg-github-bot@antfu.me>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:43:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: show each host's CPU and memory in the host pickers

The hosts dropdown at the bottom of the sidebar and the host picker in New
workspace now show each host's CPU and memory use, so you can see which
host has room before starting work there.

There was no API for it. A new daemon.get_host_stats RPC, gated on
server_info.features.hostStats, reports the CPU share in use and the used
and total memory. Inside a container the daemon reads its own cgroup, which
gives the numbers docker stats shows; elsewhere it uses the OS totals. The
app polls it every 3 s, only while a picker is open.

Fork-Change: F-17
